 director john  watts had he says the first film john  watts and i were sort of flying by the  seat of our pants this one i think we  both felt really confident so we were  able to relax we actually had so much  more fun on this one than we did on the  previous two and i'm sure that comes  down to confidence but i'm also sure  that it comes down to having a lot of  different big actors to work with in  this film if you're catching what i'm  saying alfred molina willem dafoe jamie  foxx perhaps paul giamani and of course  what we're hoping for toby maguire and  andrew garfield and hopefully they are  coming because it sounds like the future  of spider-man is kind of unknown at this  point and no way home could be it for  tom holland now i seriously doubt that  he loves playing the character and  marvel loves him and sony loves him and  they have a great relationship now and i  don't think that's coming to an end  anytime soon but in this article he's  leading us to believe like he doesn't  know what's going to happen next he said  we were all treating no way home as the  end of a franchise let's say i think if  we're lucky enough to dive into these  characters again you'd be seeing a very  different version it would no longer be  the homecoming trilogy we would give it  some time and try to build something  different and tonally change the films  whether that happens or not i don't know  but we were definitely treating no way  home like it was coming to an end and it  felt like it he goes on to say we've  been making these films for five years  now we've had such an amazing  relationship the three of us we've been  with each other every step of the way  obviously talking about zendaya and  jacob battle on and himself he continues  to say we've done every single film  every single press tour so this one  scene we didn't know if this would be  the last time we were all working  together it was heartbreaking but also  really exciting because we're all moving  into the n